    "narrative": "Our offense is anchored today by **Tyler Freeman** (64.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.78), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against mediocre pitching. **Tyler Freeman** stands out as our top play, as the 14% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against a 4.47 xERA arm provide enough leverage to overcome his lower spot in the order. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** utilizes his high-frequency contact profile to capitalize on a +11% SP skill adjustment against Michael McGreevy. While we are currently awaiting official confirmation, the stability of **Masyn Winn** (61.81) and **Dylan Beavers** (60.18) against the vulnerable Merrill Kelly and Peter Lambert, respectively, provides the necessary depth to maintain our efficiency targets across the board.\n\nThe bench decision for this slate was particularly tight, with **JJ Bleday** (49.98) narrowly missing the cut behind **Jeremiah Jackson** (49.39). While **JJ Bleday** benefits from a strong 14% park factor, his negative platoon split against Gabriel Hughes suppressed his raw score just enough to keep him on the pine. Conversely, the optimizer favored **Jeremiah Jackson** due to a more favorable situational projection, despite the lower base output. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Lawrence Butler**, who remain at risk of score volatility due to \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting orders drop, we may see a decline in their projected RBI and Run potential. With no elite arms (sub-3.00 xERA) currently threatening our primary starters, we are well-positioned to maintain our scoring floor across all 5x5 categories.",
